'i'\"; unknown value char `\"{s:q}\"` → \"Unexpected format character 'q'\" from `unpack`'s default | [ ] |\n| 143 | `json_unpack` | whitespace/separator handling: `\"{ s : i , s : i }\"`, `\"[ i , i ]\"`, `\":,: s\"` leading separators, and a multi-line format with `\\n` — assert same behaviour as compact form and correct `line`/`column`/`position` in the error for a failing variant | [ ] |\n| 144 | `json_unpack` | `\"i x\"` and `\"{s:i} i\"` → -1 \"Garbage after format string\" (post-`unpack` `next_token` check in `json_vunpack_ex`) | [ ] |\n| 145 | `json_vunpack_ex` | invoked directly with a `va_list` from a variadic wrapper: `\"{s:s%,s:[i,I,F,b,n],s:O}\"` with 12+ out-pointer varargs, `flags = 0` then `JSON_VALIDATE_ONLY` — exercises `va_copy(ap_copy, ap)` on both the success and the early-return (-1) path | [ ] |\n| 146 | `json_pack` + `json_unpack` round trip | pack a structure with `\"{s:s,s:i,s:f,s:b,s:n,s:[i,i]}\"` then unpack it with the mirrored format under `flags = 0`, `JSON_STRICT`, and `JSON_VALIDATE_ONLY`; assert `json_equal` against an independently built tree and correct refcounts after `json_decref` | [ ] |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e1728859-25d0-4463-adf4-96231e8435a5","uuid":"d2523fba-d39b-4aa3-9ebf-c54b58778b15","timestamp":"2026-08-31T03:49:48.857Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Differential-test configurations, part 2: `value.c` + `pack_unpack.c`\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n| 1 | `json_object` | fresh empty object; assert `json_typeof == JSON_OBJECT`, `refcount == 1`, `json_object_size == 0`; hashtable starts at order 3 (8 buckets) | [ ] |\n| 2 | `json_object`, `json_object_seed` | first-ever `json_object()` call with `hashtable_seed == 0` so the autoseed path (`json_object_seed(0)`) runs; then a second `json_object()` that skips autoseed | [ ] |\n| 3 | `json_array` | fresh empty array