ket (same hash modulo bucket count), replace the value of an existing key, delete the first / middle / last / only element, delete a key that is absent, iterate a table while deleting the current element, iterate an empty table, and use keys that are empty / very long / contain embedded NUL / are arbitrary binary bytes. Note that key comparison uses key_len so `\"ab\\0cd\"` and `\"ab\"` are distinct keys.\n\nhashtable_seed.c — `hashtable_seed`, `json_object_seed`: seed 0 (triggers random seed generation) vs a fixed non-zero seed; calling json_object_seed twice; the effect of the seed on bucket assignment and therefore on iteration order; the buffer/entropy source branches (USE_URANDOM etc.) visible in the source.\n\nstrconv.c — `jsonp_strtod`, `jsonp_dtostr`. Read strconv.c carefully and enumerate every branch. For `jsonp_dtostr` cover: the `prec` argument at 0 and 1..17 and beyond 17, the exponent-rewriting branch, the trailing-`.0`/integral-value branch, the trailing-zero handling, the `size` argument at exactly-fits and too-small, and values 0.0 / -0.0 / subnormal / 1e308 / 1e-308 / integral-valued / doubles needing all 17 significant digits. For `jsonp_strtod` cover inputs supplied via a strbuffer: plain integer text, fraction, exponent in both cases and signs, values that overflow to inf (ERANGE), values that underflow to 0, and the locale-independent decimal-point handling.\n\ndtoa.c exported entry points — `dtoa` and `dtoa_r` with `mode` 0..9 crossed with `ndigits` 0, 1, 5, 17, 30, over a fixed set of doubles including 0.0, -0.0, subnormals, powers of two, 1e308, 1e-308, and values needing 17 digits; check the returned string, `*decpt`, `*sign` and `*rve`. `dtoa_r` additionally with a caller-supplied buffer that is large enough and that is too small. `freedtoa` on a `dtoa` result. `gethex` with hex-float strings (\"0x1p0\", \"0x1.8p3\", \"0x.8p1\", malformed/no-digits/no-exponent forms) crossed with `rounding` 0..3 and `sign` 0/1, checking the returned code and the updated string pointer. `strtod__unused` with numeric strings, hex floats, inf/nan spellings, overflow/underflow, and trailing garbage (verify the endptr). Also the exported data symbol `dtoa_divmax`.\n\nThe \"configuration\" cell must be concrete enough to write a randomized differential test from. Number rows sequentially from 1. Aim for 60-90 rows.\n\nWhen done, run `wc -l` and `grep -c '^| [0-9]'` and report both numbers."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2848,"cache_read_input_tokens":116931,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2848,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e1728859-25d0-4463-adf4-96231e8435a5","uuid":"0e3945d8-a36c-4ab2-8e92-e36632b88a1b","timestamp":"2026-08-31T03:50:49.243Z"}
