 [ \\t\\r\\n ] \\t\\r\\n } \\t\\r\\n \"`. Drives the `lex_scan` skip loop `c==' '||'\\t'||'\\n'||'\\r'` (load.c:572-574). Assert same value as whitespace-free form. | [ ] |\n| 7 | `json_loads` | flags=0; trailing whitespace only after a complete document: `{\"a\":1}\\n\\t\\r ` — EOF check runs, `lex_scan` consumes whitespace and returns `TOKEN_EOF`, so parse succeeds (load.c:867-874). | [ ] |\n| 8 | `json_loads` | flags=0; trailing non-whitespace: `{\"a\":1} garbage` and `[1,2] [3]` — EOF check enabled, expect NULL and `json_error_end_of_input_expected`. | [ ] |\n| 9 | `json_loads` | flags=`JSON_DISABLE_EOF_CHECK`; input `{\"a\":1} garbage` and `[1,2]}}}` — EOF check skipped (load.c:867), expect success with only the first value returned; trailing bytes ignored. | [ ] |\n| 10 | `json_loads` | flags=`JSON_DISABLE_EOF_CHECK`; input `{\"a\":1}   ` (trailing whitespace) — assert identical result to flags=0 case (row 7): flag must not change the value. | [ ] |\n| 11 | `json_loads` | flags=`JSON_DISABLE_EOF_CHECK`; multiple concatenated values `[1][2][3]` — assert only `[1]` is returned and `error->position` is NOT set (the `if (error)` position write at load.c:877-880 still runs; assert position equals bytes consumed for the first value). | [ ] |\n| 12 | `json_loads` | flags=0; multiple concatenated values `[1][2]` — expect failure (contrast with row 11), error code `json_error_end_of_input_expected`. | [ ] |\n| 13 | `json_loads` | flags=0; duplicate keys `{\"a\":1,\"a\":2,\"a\":3}` — `JSON_REJECT_DUPLICATES` off, `json_object_setn_new_nocheck` overwrites (load.c:713); assert success, size 1, `a == 3` (LAST wins). | [ ] |\n| 14 | `json_loads` | flags=`JSON_REJECT_DUPLICATES`; input `{\"a\":1,\"a\":2}` — `json_object_getn` hit (load.c:691-697); expect NULL and `json_error_duplicate_key`. | [ ] |\n| 15 | `json_loads` | flags=`JSON_REJECT_DUPLICATES`; input `{\"a\":1,\"b\":2}` (no duplicates) — assert identical result to flags=0. | [ ] |\n| 16 | `json_loads` | flags=`JSON_R