and 1..17, hard doubles, forced `.0`, `MAX_REAL_STR_LENGTH`/`MAX_INTEGER_STR_LENGTH` overflow arms.\n- Rows 54-60: `JSON_EMBED` — capture-then-clear semantics on arrays, objects, empty containers, scalars, and crossed with INDENT/COMPACT.\n- Rows 61-67: meaningful combinations, including the full 80-config indent × compact × ascii × sort × slash cross-product.\n- Rows 68-72: input-shape branches (`n == 1` vs the `n-1` comma loop, `if (next)` object arm, deep nesting, every `switch` case at depth 0 and 1).\n- Rows 73-88: entry points — `json_dumpb` with larger/exact/smaller/zero buffer (including the non-prefix partial-copy quirk where `dump_to_buffer` skips an oversized chunk but still copies a later small one), `json_dumpf`/`json_dumpfd`/`json_dump_file` success and failure (`fwrite != 1`, short `write`, `fopen`/`fclose` failure), and `json_dump_callback` failing on the first/middle/last chunk with a systematic sweep of every `return -1` propagation site, the `jsonp_free(keys)` cleanup paths, and circular-reference detection.\n\nTwo findings worth flagging for the port: the `case '/'` arm in `dump_string` is unreachable unless `JSON_ESCAPE_SLASH` is set, and `dump_string`'s return value is **ignored** at both key-dumping call sites (sorted and unsorted), so a callback failure on a key string is silently swallowed until the next `dump` call. Also `json_dumpb` returning 0 is ambiguous between error and legitimately-empty output (`JSON_EMBED` on `[]`).","usage":{"total_tokens":41489,"tool_uses":12,"duration_ms":221059},"uuid":"83c8bd32-a128-427e-95d9-e7ca1826b743","session_id":"e1728859-25d0-4463-adf4-96231e8435a5"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_toy7bbj3nje56mvb2qsg3a6hy7dvqx6ugy24bqj3n5x3mmcgmabq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. `translation/ERRORS.md` is written.\n\n## Verification numbers\n- `wc -l ERRORS.md` → **403 lines**\n- `grep -c '^| [0-9]' ERRORS.md` → **356 rows** (numbering verified strictly sequential 1…356)\n- **110 distinct exported functions** named in the `function` column\n\n## What was done\nRead `jansson.h`, `jansson_private.h`, `jansson_config.h`, `jansson_private_config.h`, and every `.c` in `c_src/src/` (dtoa.c limited to the paths reachable from `dtoa`/`dtoa_r`/`gethex`/`freedtoa`/`jsonp_dtostr`/`jsonp_strtod`). Then I **compiled three probe programs against `c_src/build/libjansson.so`** and executed them, so the \"expected C result\" column carries real observed values (return value + `json_error_code` numeric + exact `text`/`source`/`line`/`column`/`position`) rather than inferred ones.\n\n## Key findings worth flagging to the porter\n- **`json_error_code` values are the literal enum ordinals stored in `text[159]`** — the table lists them numerically (e.g. `6` = premature_end_of_input) because that's what a test reads.\n- **Error structs are sticky**: `jsonp_error_vset` silently drops any second error, so e.g. `json_pack(\"{s:s}\",\"k\",NULL)` reports `\"NULL string\"`, *not* `\"NULL object value\"`. A port that overwrites will fail parity.\n- **`invalid_syntax` is silently upgraded to `premature_end_of_input`** in `error_set` whenever there is no saved lexer text — this is why `\"[1,2\"` yields code 6 and `\"[1 2]\"` yields code 8 with otherwise-identical messages.\n- **Real-number dumping fails at `JSON_REAL_PRECISION(n)` for `n >= 22`** on `json_real(0.1)` (verified): 22–24 hit the `jsonp_dtostr` length check, ≥25 hit `dtoa_r`'s short-buffer `NULL`. `MAX_REAL_STR_LENGTH` is only 25.\n- **Self-insertion (`json == value`) is rejected**, so a direct `a=[a]` cycle is impossible; the circular-reference paths in `json_dumps`/`json_deep_copy` need an *indirect* cycle (`a=[b]`, `b=[a]`) — verified NULL.\n- **`json_dumpb` returns `0` on error**, which is indistinguishable from an empty dump; **`json_dumpb` with a too-small buffer is not an error** and returns the required size.\n- **Two swallowed-error bugs**: `dump_string`'s return value for object *keys* is ignored in both the sorted and unsorted `do_dump` branches (rows 352–353).\n- **`json_pack(\"s*\", NULL)` / `json_pack(\"o*\", NULL)` return `NULL` with no error recorded** — `json_error_code` reads uninitialised memory, as does the `lex_init`-OOM path. Tests must not assert on the code there (called out in Notes).\n- **`hashtable_set`'s key-length overflow guard is dead code**: `hash_str` reads the key before `init_pair` runs, so a huge `key_len` segfaults first (confirmed by an actual SIGSEGV).\n- `dtoa.c`'s asserts compile to nothing (`#define assert(x)` without `DEBUG`), but load.c/dump.c/strconv.c asserts **are** live — `CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE` is empty, so no `-DNDEBUG`. `jsonp_strtod`'s assert is genuinely reachable via direct FFI call.\n\nThe Notes section lists every path that is only reachable on malloc failure, only reachable as a crash, or provably unreachable (all `assert`s, `json_equal`/`json_copy`/`do_dump` `default:` arms, `decode_unicode_escape`'s second-pass failure, `strtod__unused`, `gethex`), with the reason for each."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":573,"cache_read_input_tokens":210472,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":573,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_014y9ju9E2WVP556Hjr8HmH8","session_id":"e1728859-25d0-4463-adf4-96231e8435a5","uuid":"d5cf2834-8582-47f7-8185-a84e39fb892d","timestamp":"2026-08-31T03:54:05.269Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Derive ERRORS.md from C source"}
