{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_2ztfwjxtdoyrbt5xxqj65mfxonu3zqttza3fe6mtplvs75ymqzza","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_013BJBaiv9nxRGKwiqwYGCha","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-6oQ0Bh/translation/CONFIGS_part3.md <<'EOF'\n| 21 | `hashtable_del` (last of a chain) | 3+ keys in one bucket; delete the **first-inserted** one (which is `bucket->last`) → `bucket->last = pair->list.prev` branch; assert the remaining chain terminates correctly (`hashtable_find_pair` stops at the new `bucket->last`) and a lookup for the deleted key returns NULL | [ ] |\n| 22 | `hashtable_del` (absent key) | (a) key hashing to an empty bucket, (b) key hashing to a non-empty bucket but not present, (c) same bytes but wrong `key_len`, (d) delete on an empty table → each returns **-1**, size unchanged, no `json_decref` performed (verify the value's refcount of a same-named live object is untouched) | [ ] |\n| 23 | `hashtable_del` (delete-all then reinsert) | insert 20 keys (order grows to 5), delete all 20 one by one → size 0 but `order` stays 5 (no shrink), every bucket back to `first==last==&ht->list`; then insert 20 fresh keys and assert no rehash occurs until size again reaches 32 | [ ] |\n| 24 | `hashtable_clear` | table with 12 entries at `order==4`; `hashtable_clear` → all values decref'd, size 0, `list`/`ordered_list` reinitialised, **all 16 buckets** reset (loop uses the *current* order, not the initial one), `order` stays 4; then reuse the table (set/get/iter) and finally `hashtable_close` | [ ] |\n| 25 | `hashtable_clear` on empty table | `hashtable_init` then `hashtable_clear` immediately (empty `hashtable_do_clear` loop) then `hashtable_clear` again; assert idempotent and table still usable | [ ] |\n| 26 | `hashtable_iter` + `hashtable_iter_next` | 5 entries; full walk: `hashtable_iter` → e0, then `hashtable_iter_next` 5 times, the 5th retur