\"0x1.8p+3\"`, `\"0x1.8p-3\"`→1.5/8, `\"0x.8p1\"`→1.0, `\"0x8p-3\"`→1.0, `\"0x10p0\"`→16.0, `\"0x0001p0\"` (leading-zero skip loop `while(s0[havedig]=='0') havedig++`), `\"0xABCDEFp0\"`, `\"0xabcdefp0\"`, `\"0x1P4\"` (uppercase P). Assert the resulting double bits, that `*sp` points just past the consumed text, and `errno` unchanged. | [ ] |\n| 76 | `gethex` zero / all-zero-mantissa (`zret`) | `\"0x0\"`, `\"0x0p0\"`, `\"0x0.0\"`, `\"0x0.0p99\"`, `\"0x00000\"`, `\"0x.0\"`, `\"0x0.000p-99\"`. All take `zret = 1` → `retz1` → `rvp->d = 0.` with **errno NOT set** (retz1 is jumped to before `Set_errno`). Assert `+0.0` bits (sign is applied by the caller, not by gethex) and the final `*sp`. | [ ] |\n| 77 | `gethex` malformed input (`!havedig` endptr rollback) | `\"0x\"`, `\"0xp0\"`, `\"0xg\"`, `\"0x.\"`, `\"0x.p3\"`, `\"0x.g\"`, `\"0x\"` followed by NUL. When no hex digit is found, `*sp = (char*)s0 - 1`, i.e. the endptr is rolled back to point at the `'x'` so the caller reports a value of `0` consumed as just `\"0\"`. Assert the exact `*sp` offset relative to the input start for each case, and `rvp->d == 0.0`. | [ ] |\n| 78 | `gethex` malformed exponent (`s = s1` rollback) | `\"0x1p\"`, `\"0x1p+\"`, `\"0x1p-\"`, `\"0x1pz\"`, `\"0x1p+z\"`, `\"0x1.8p\"`. The `switch(*s){case 'p':}` arm checks `(n = hexdig[*s]) == 0 || n > 0x19` (i.e. not a decimal digit) and resets `s = s1`, so the `p` and any sign are **not** consumed. Assert the value is the mantissa-only result (`1.0`, `1.5`) and `*sp` points at the `'p'`. | [ ] |\n| 79 | `gethex` `big` exponent (overflow) × `rounding` × `sign` | Inputs `\"0x1p99999999999\"`, `\"0x1p2147483648\"` (exponent accumulation sets `big = 1` when `e1 & 0xf8000000`). Cross `rounding` ∈ {0=Round_zero, 1=Round_near, 2=Round_up, 3=Round_down} × `sign` ∈ {0,1}. Expected per the `if (big) { ... switch(rounding) }` block: `Round_near` → `ovfl1` (errno ERANGE, `word0 = Exp_mask`, `word1 = 0` → +inf); `Round_up` with `sign==0` → ovfl1, with `sign==1` → `r