{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_xb37dvh43shjpyrcnozuha244zpccg6vmqmwtmmzvbppg6i3yxkq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_019aLJXHkzM6g67cTn5RRNt3","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Phase B tests for load.c","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"Working dir: /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-6oQ0Bh\n\nYou are writing DIFFERENTIAL tests that compare the C jansson library against its Rust translation through the FFI boundary. The C in `c_src/` is ALWAYS correct ground truth. NEVER modify anything in `c_src/`. On any divergence you MUST fix the RUST source in `translation/src/` — never change the C and never weaken the test to match the Rust.\n\nSTEP 1 — read these first:\n- `translation/tests/HARNESS.md` — the complete test-harness API contract. Follow it exactly.\n- `translation/tests/a03_hashtable.rs` — a worked example of the style expected.\n- `c_src/src/load.c` and the decoding flag macros in `c_src/include/jansson.h`.\n- `translation/CONFIGS.md` rows **89 through 163** (section \"B. Decoding — load.c\"). These are your required coverage.\n\nSTEP 2 — write `translation/tests/a07_load.rs`.\nCover EVERY one of CONFIGS.md rows 89-163. Requirements:\n- Use `mod common; use common::*;` and `let (c, r) = both();` exactly as HARNESS.md describes.\n- Use the seeded `Rng` for MANY randomized inputs per configuration (at least ~200 iterations per flag combination), not one hand-picked value. Give each test its own fixed seed constant.\n- For each input text + flags: call BOTH `json_loads` variants, then compare (a) whether the result was NULL, (b) the full `json_error_t` byte image via `.raw()` (this catches line/column/position/text/code divergence), and (c) when parsing succeeded, a canonical re-dump of the parsed tree via `json_dumps(.., JSON_SORT_KEYS | JSON_ENCODE_ANY)` compared with `cbytes(...)` byte-for-byte.\n- Write a generator that emits random VALID json text (all 8 types, all escape forms `\\\" \\\\ \\/ \\b \\f \\n \\r \\t \\uXXXX`, valid surrogate pairs, raw 2/3/4-byte UTF-8, every number form: integer/negative/fraction/exponent with e|E and +|-|bare, big and small exponents, int64 boundary values), and a second generator that emits random MALFORMED json (truncated, bad escapes, lone surrogates, trailing garbage, unclosed containers, bad number forms).\n- Exercise ALL decoding entry points, not just `json_loads`: `json_loadb` (buflen shorter than the string, exactly the string, and 0), `json_loadf` (a real `FILE*` via `fopen` on a temp path — get a temp dir from the `TMPDIR` env var), `json_loadfd` (a real fd), `json_load_file`, and `json_load_callback` (callbacks that return 0 immediately, that feed 1 byte at a time, that feed large chunks, and that stop short partway through).\n- Cover the decoding flags individually AND combined: `JSON_REJECT_DUPLICATES`, `JSON_DISABLE_EOF_CHECK`, `JSON_DECODE_ANY`, `JSON_DECODE_INT_AS_REAL`, `JSON_ALLOW_NUL`. Include the combination rows the CONFIGS table calls for.\n- Include the nesting-depth rows: depth 1, a few, exactly JSON_PARSER_MAX_DEPTH (2048), and one past it — both must agree on where the stack-overflow rejection kicks in.\n- Include round-trip rows: load, dump, load again, assert stability across both libraries.\n- Free every value with `decref(api, j)` and every dumped buffer with `jfree(api, ptr)`.\n\nSTEP 3 — run it: `cd translation && timeout 600 cargo test --release --test a07_load 2>&1 | tail -40`\nIterate until it passes. `--release` is required; cargo is offline-configured already.\n\nSTEP 4 — on ANY divergence: read the corresponding C in `c_src/src/load.c`, find the matching Rust in `translation/src/load.rs` (or strconv.rs/utf.rs/value.rs), and FIX THE RUST so it matches the C exactly. Re-run.\n\nSTEP 5 — edit `translation/CONFIGS.md` and change `[ ]` to `[x]` for each of rows 89-163 your tests now cover and pass. Only check rows that genuinely pass.\n\nReport at the end: the test count, pass/fail status, every Rust bug you fixed (file + short before/after), and which CONFIGS rows you checked off."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4677,"cache_read_input_tokens":164870,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4677,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e1728859-25d0-4463-adf4-96231e8435a5","uuid":"a21a9a0c-9621-4235-a112-00ec3f82e3ff","timestamp":"2026-08-31T03:55:33.464Z"}
