that dump.c must ignore: `flags = 0x800` (between ESCAPE_SLASH and the precision field — actually part of `REAL_PRECISION`, so verify it *does* change real output), `flags = 0x20000`, `flags = SIZE_MAX`. Documents which bits are live: `0x1F`, `0x20`, `0x40`, `0x80`, `0x200`, `0x400`, `0xF800`, `0x10000`. | [ ] |\n80\t| 68 | `json_dumps` | `flags = 0`, input array of 1 element `[1]`. `n == 1`, so the `for (i = 0; i < n - 1; ++i)` loop body never executes and `i == 0` falls through to the single trailing `do_dump(json_array_get(json, i), ...)`. Boundary between the \"loop\" and \"last element\" code paths. | [ ] |\n81\t| 69 | `json_dumps` | `flags = 0`, arrays of 2 and of many (≥ 16) elements. The 2-element case runs the comma loop exactly once; the many case exercises it repeatedly. Pair with `JSON_INDENT(2)` to check comma+indent ordering (`dump(\",\")` then `dump_indent`). | [ ] |\n82\t| 70 | `json_dumps` | `flags = 0`, object with 1 key vs 2 keys vs many (≥ 16) keys, unsorted branch. 1-key: `next == NULL` on the first iteration → closing `dump_indent(flags, depth, 0, ...)`. Multi-key: the `if (next)` comma arm. Mirrors row 68/69 for the object path. | [ ] |\n83\t| 71 | `json_dumps` | `flags = JSON_INDENT(2)`, document nested 5+ levels mixing arrays and objects: `{\"a\":[{\"b\":[{\"c\":[1,[2,{\"d\":{}}]]}]}]}`. Verifies `depth` increments once per `do_dump` recursion for both container kinds and that the empty innermost `{}` still emits no interior whitespace. | [ ] |\n84\t| 72 | `json_dumps` | `flags = JSON_ENCODE_ANY` on all 8 `json_type` values at top level in one sweep (`JSON_OBJECT`, `JSON_ARRAY`, `JSON_STRING`, `JSON_INTEGER`, `JSON_REAL`, `JSON_TRUE`, `JSON_FALSE`, `JSON_NULL`) and as the *sole element* of an array and *sole value* of an object. Covers every `case` of the `switch (json_typeof(json))` at depth 0 and depth 1; the `default:` arm is unreachable for well-formed values. | [ ] |\n85\t| 73 | `json_dumpb` | `flags = 0`, input `[1,2,3]` (needed size 9