and `JSON_EMBED`. | [ ] |\n101\t\n102\t## B. Decoding — load.c\n103\t\n104\t| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n105\t|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n106\t| 89 | `json_loads` | flags=0; input `{}` — empty object; `parse_object` takes the early-return `lex->token=='}'` path (load.c:668). Assert object, size 0, EOF check passes. | [ ] |\n107\t| 90 | `json_loads` | flags=0; input `[]` — empty array; `parse_array` early-return `lex->token==']'` (load.c:745). Assert array, size 0. | [ ] |\n108\t| 91 | `json_loads` | flags=0; input `{\"a\":1}` — 1-member object; one pass of the `while(1)` loop, loop exits via `lex->token != ','` then `'}'` check (load.c:721-730). | [ ] |\n109\t| 92 | `json_loads` | flags=0; input `{\"a\":1,\"b\":2,\"c\":3}` — many members; 3 loop iterations, comma branch taken twice. Assert insertion order preserved on `json_object_iter`. | [ ] |\n110\t| 93 | `json_loads` | flags=0; input `[1]` then `[1,2,3,4,5]` — 1 vs many elements; exercises `parse_array` comma branch (load.c:757-761). Assert array sizes and element order. | [ ] |\n111\t| 94 | `json_loads` | flags=0; input with every whitespace form between every token: `\" \\t\\r\\n{ \\t\\r\\n \\\"a\\\" \\t\\r\\n : \\t\\r\\n 1 \\t\\r\\n , \\t\\r\\n \\\"b\\\" \\t\\r\\n : \\t\\r\\n [ \\t\\r\\n ] \\t\\r\\n } \\t\\r\\n \"`. Drives the `lex_scan` skip loop `c==' '||'\\t'||'\\n'||'\\r'` (load.c:572-574). Assert same value as whitespace-free form. | [ ] |\n112\t| 95 | `json_loads` | flags=0; trailing whitespace only after a complete document: `{\"a\":1}\\n\\t\\r ` — EOF check runs, `lex_scan` consumes whitespace and returns `TOKEN_EOF`, so parse succeeds (load.c:867-874). | [ ] |\n113\t| 96 | `json_loads` | flags=0; trailing non-whitespace: `{\"a\":1} garbage` and `[1,2] [3]` — EOF check enabled, expect NULL and `json_error_end_of_input_expected`. | [ ] |\n114\t| 97 | `json_loads` | flags=`JSON_DISABLE_EOF_CHECK`; input `{\"a\":1