{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_sz2qw3gds7s5omecsb6vkdvzjhg63syaqimttvki62ttlq5axmaq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done.\n\n## Result\n\n**`translation/tests/a07_load.rs`** — 22 tests, **all passing** (`cargo test --release --test a07_load`). ~47,400 full three-way differential comparisons across the run (each comparison = NULL-ness + full `json_error_t` byte image + canonical re-dump).\n\nEvery comparison checks, for the same bytes and same flags on both `.so`s:\n1. returned NULL or not,\n2. `json_error_t::raw()` — the whole 252-byte image, started from `poisoned()` so \"did not write\" is distinguishable from \"wrote NUL\"; this pins line/column/position/source/text/code at once,\n3. `json_dumps(.., JSON_SORT_KEYS | JSON_ENCODE_ANY)` compared byte-for-byte via `cbytes`.\n\nEvery `json_t` freed with `decref(api, …)`, every dump buffer with `jfree(api, …)`.\n\n### Coverage\n- **Generators**: valid-JSON generator (all 8 types, all short escapes `\\\" \\\\ \\/ \\b \\f \\n \\r \\t`, `\\uXXXX` in every `utf8_encode` width, valid surrogate pairs, raw 2/3/4-byte UTF-8, every number form incl. `e|E`, `+|-|bare`, big/small exponents, int64 boundary and one-past values); malformed generator (67 hand-written cases + 10 mutation kinds: truncate, delete/flip/insert byte, trailing garbage, stripped closers, injected bad escape/lone surrogate/bad number, raw control chars).\n- **Flag sweep**: 12 flag sets (each flag alone and the combinations rows 107/114/126/151/152/153 call for, plus the all-five combination), ≥200–250 iterations each.\n- **All six entry points**: `json_loads`, `json_loadb` (buflen 0 / short / exact / cutting a multi-byte sequence / embedded NUL), `json_loadf` (real `FILE*` via `fopen` on `$TMPDIR`), `json_loadfd` (real fd), `json_load_file` (incl. missing path → `cannot_open_file`, and source-path lengths straddling the 80-byte `jsonp_error_set_source` truncation), `json_load_callback` (returns 0 immediately, returns `(size_t)-1`, 1 byte/call, large chunks, stops short at 1/4·1/2·3/4·full — plus callback-invocation-count and bytes-consumed compared).\n- **Nesting**: depths 1/2/3/5/10/50/100, exactly 2048, 2049, and the row-157 off-by-one (2048 brackets + scalar fails, 2047 + scalar succeeds), for array/object/mixed shapes; run on a 256 MB-stack thread.\n- **Round trips**: load → canonical dump → load → dump, asserted a fixed point in each library and identical across them, plus `json_equal(original, reloaded)`; and the same document through every entry point.\n- **Extra stress** (beyond the rows): the `saved_text.length <= 20` error-context gate at every token length 1–40, 40 KB tokens, multi-byte column tracking / `last_column` restore on ungotten `'\\n'`, and EOF landing inside a partial 2/3/4-byte sequence at every cut offset.\n\n### Rust bugs fixed\n**None — no divergence was found.** Every one of the ~47k comparisons matched byte-for-byte. The four initial test failures were all *my* wrong ground-truth expectations, corrected against the C:\n- `1e-5`/`1.5e-5`, not `1e-05` (jansson's `jsonp_dtostr` strips exponent zero padding).\n- `[1,]` → `\"unexpected token near ']'\"` (the `]` reaches `parse_value`'s `default:`), not `\"']' expected\"`.\n- A bad UTF-8 byte *inside a string* keeps its `\" near '…'\"` context; the no-context path (`load.c:122-124`) needs an empty `saved_text`, so I added `\\x80`/`\\xff`/`\\xc0\\x41` as whole documents to cover it.\n- The 2048-deep dump is `\"[\"*2048 + \"]\"*2048`.\n\nI also had to cap the long-path test at 200 padding chars (255-byte filename limit).\n\nNothing in `c_src/` was touched, and `translation/src/` needed no change.\n\n### CONFIGS.md\nChecked off **rows 89–163** (all 75 rows of section \"B. Decoding — load.c\"); verified none were left unchecked. Note: `translation/tests/a05_strconv_dtoa.rs` (a concurrent agent's file) aborts with `free(): invalid pointer` when the whole suite runs — unrelated to this work, but it will break `cargo test --release` / `run_tests.sh` until fixed."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":194,"cache_read_input_tokens":202329,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":194,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_019aLJXHkzM6g67cTn5RRNt3","session_id":"e1728859-25d0-4463-adf4-96231e8435a5","uuid":"7ba60a6f-c413-4f0d-b56e-5f6dfc4292bd","timestamp":"2026-08-31T04:11:10.778Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Phase B tests for load.c"}
