{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_b337uz6w7nfhrxkchz3sqjhhfdcdktkduirznhmrdtaksg4n5y2q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All green. Final summary of the work:\n\n## Test file: `translation/tests/a12_errors_dump.rs` (15 tests, 15 passing)\n\n| test | ERRORS.md rows |\n|---|---|\n| `rows_200_201_203_encode_any_gate_and_null_json` | 200, 201, 203 + NULL `json` through all 6 entry points |\n| `null_callback_pointer_on_the_paths_that_never_dereference_it` | FFI boundary (no row) |\n| `rows_198_202_210_allocation_failure_budget_sweep` | 198, 202, 210 |\n| `rows_199_204_211_352_353_callback_failure_key_vs_value` | 199, 204, 211, 352, 353 |\n| `rows_205_206_circular_references_every_entry_point` | 205, 206 (+ DAGs must succeed) |\n| `row_207_invalid_utf8_string_value_aborts_the_dump` | 207 |\n| `rows_352_353_invalid_utf8_object_key_is_silently_emitted` | 352, 353 |\n| `rows_208_209_real_precision_makes_dtostr_fail` | 208, 209 |\n| `rows_212_213_json_dumpb_zero_is_ambiguous` | 212, 213 |\n| `rows_214_215_216_217_218_file_and_fd_failures` | 214–218 |\n| `row_219_integer_snprintf_can_never_overflow_the_buffer` | 219 (documenting) |\n| `row_220_corrupted_type_reaches_the_default_arm` | 220 |\n| `rows_350_351_sort_keys_asserts_are_unreachable_invariants` | 350, 351 (documenting) |\n| `row_354_failed_shrink_realloc_returns_the_larger_buffer` | 354 (success, not failure) |\n| `rows_355_356_undefined_flag_bits_are_ignored_identically` | 356 |\n\nNotable techniques: a budgeted `malloc` hook (installed on both libs via `json_set_alloc_funcs2`, always restored) walks the four allocation sites of a dump in order — the assertion that the first succeeding budget with `JSON_SORT_KEYS` is **exactly one higher** than without it is what proves row 210 was actually reached; malloc/realloc *call counts* are also compared between the libraries. A callback that fails on a chunk selected **by content** (not index) expresses the 352/353 asymmetry: failing on the key's quote/body → dump returns **0** (swallowed), the identical failure on the value's quote/body → **-1**. Row 354 uses an always-failing `realloc` with outputs ≤ 14 bytes so the initial 16-byte strbuffer never grows, isolating the trailing shrink. Row 220 uses a stack `json_t { type_: 99, refcount: usize::MAX }` (the `(size_t)-1` refcount makes it a never-freed singleton, so it can safely be embedded in real containers).\n\n## Rust bug fixed — `translation/src/dump.rs` (`do_dump`)\n\nBefore, the callback was unwrapped as the **first** statement, so `json_dump_callback(NULL, NULL_callback, d, JSON_ENCODE_ANY)` — which the C answers `-1` from `if (!json) return -1;` without ever touching `dump` — panicked in Rust and, with `panic = \"abort\"`, killed the process:\n\n```rust\nlet dumpf = dump.unwrap();          // <-- panicked before the NULL check\nlet embed = flags & JSON_EMBED;\nflags &= ~JSON_EMBED;\nif json.is_null() { return -1; }\nmatch json_typeof(json) { ...\n```\n\nAfter: the null check runs first, and the type is validated against `JSON_OBJECT..=JSON_NULL` before `dump.unwrap()`, so the C's `!json` path *and* its `default:` arm (row 220) both return `-1` with a NULL callback exactly as the C does. Everything else is unchanged. `strconv.rs` needed no changes.\n\n## ERRORS.md rows marked `[-]`\n\n- **219** — unreachable: `%lld` of a `json_int_t` is at most 20 chars, always < `MAX_INTEGER_STR_LENGTH` (25), and glibc's `snprintf` cannot fail on an integer conversion, so neither disjunct of `size < 0 || size >= 25` can ever be true. Replaced with a passing invariant test (every `i64` including both extremes, all 19 decimal widths, 400 random values, all render in < 25 bytes).\n- **350** / **351** — live `assert(i == size)` / `assert(value)` → SIGABRT, and unreachable (the key array is filled straight from the object's own iterator). Instead of a fake assertion, the test verifies the invariants each assert encodes *through the FFI* (iterated key count == `json_object_size`, and every harvested key is findable with `json_object_getn`) for the awkward key shapes — empty, embedded NUL, invalid UTF-8, 11 keys forcing a rehash — and compares them between libraries.\n\nAll other assigned rows (198–218, 220, 352, 353, 354, 356) are now `[x]`. Row 355 was left untouched (not assigned), though the flag-masking test does cover its claim for the encoder.\n\n## Regression / cross-checks\n\n`cargo test --release --test a06_dump` → 23/23 pass. Full suite also passes, with one exception that is **not** mine: `a08_pack_unpack::hand_built_va_list_is_abi_correct` failed on a later run in which a08's test count had grown from 63 to 64 between two invocations — i.e. the concurrently-edited `pack_unpack` work in flight, not something `dump.rs` can influence. No suspected bugs outside `dump.rs` were found on the dump error surface."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":423,"cache_read_input_tokens":197809,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":423,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_013vS8kQHFk8DCEET4qNhUpR","session_id":"e1728859-25d0-4463-adf4-96231e8435a5","uuid":"a30e220a-cc37-4f86-9544-53fde4c5885a","timestamp":"2026-08-31T04:40:20.933Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Phase C error tests for dump.c"}
