{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_foarscbxqbk6zdxy6xu5e5ojc7lpf763rdoddfvkn5lkal3x37iq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`translation/tests/a08_pack_unpack.rs` is written and passing.\n\n## Result\n\n**71 tests, all passing**, 0 warnings, ~2.5s sequential / ~0.8s parallel.\n\n```\ncd translation && cargo test --release --test a08_pack_unpack\ntest result: ok. 71 passed; 0 failed\n```\n\n## Rust bugs fixed: none\n\nI found **zero divergences** between `c_src/src/pack_unpack.c` and `translation/src/pack_unpack.rs` / `varargs.rs`. Both files are byte-faithful under everything I could throw at them, so neither was modified. Coverage that backs that up:\n\n- Every pack format char + modifier: `{ [ s n b i I f O o` × `# % + ? *`, including the special-cased combos `s#`, `s%`, `s+`, `s+#`, `s#+#`, `s+%`, `s%+%`, `s#+%`, `s%+#`, `s#+#+#`, `s?`, `s*`, `s?#`/`s?%`/`s?+`/`s*#` (the \"Cannot use '%c' on optional strings\" guard), `o?`/`O?`/`o*`/`O*`, keys via every `read_string` variant, and modifiers in key/value/element position.\n- Every unpack format char: `{ [ s i I b f F O o n` × `! * ? %`, the full `unpack_value_starters` = `\"{[siIbfFOon\"` gate (each accepted, plus rejected chars), trailing `!`/`*` in both containers, and tokens after `!`/`*`.\n- All three `json_error_t` sources: `<args>`, `<format>`, `<validation>`, `<root>` **and `<internal>`** — the last via a thread-local \"fail exactly 16-byte (`STRBUFFER_MIN_SIZE`) allocations\" hook installed with `json_set_alloc_funcs2`. The hooks forward to libc and the failure switch is thread-local, so concurrent tests in the same binary are unaffected.\n- Poisoned out-pointer blocks (`Slots`, 24 slots × 6 types, sentinel `char*`/`json_t*` that are safe to read back) compared as a whole after every unpack, plus refcount checks for every `o`/`O`.\n- `JSON_VALIDATE_ONLY` / `JSON_STRICT` alone and together, with and without `?` keys, and the explicit proof that trailing `*` sets `strict = -1` and **suppresses** the `JSON_STRICT` promotion (C returns 0 where plain `JSON_STRICT` returns -1).\n- `json_vpack_ex` / `json_vunpack_ex` / `json_vsprintf` / `jsonp_error_vset` through `vashim()`, on success and early-error paths.\n- The naked-asm variadic prologues in `varargs.rs` driven directly with 8 ints + 10 doubles + 2 pointers so both register save areas overflow, for all six entry points (`gp_offset` 8/16/24/32/48).\n- `json_sprintf`/`json_vsprintf` across `%s %d %i %f %g %e %E %G %x %X %o %u %c %%`, width/precision/flag variants (`%5.2f`, `%-10s`, `%05d`, `%+.3e`, …), 10 KiB output, `%.4000f`, invalid UTF-8 → NULL, and the empty format.\n- ~1M randomized cases. Because Rust cannot build a variadic call of run-time arity, the randomized generators build a **real x86-64 SysV `va_list` by hand** (`gp_offset=48`, `fp_offset=176` → all args from a controlled `overflow_arg_area`) from a plan generated together with the format, so format and varargs always match. `hand_built_va_list_is_abi_correct` pins this against a compiler-built `va_list` through the shim.\n\n## C behaviours worth recording (no action needed)\n\n- `s%` + `JSON_VALIDATE_ONLY` is a **format error**, not a validation pass: the whole `case 's'` body is skipped so the `%` is never consumed and `unpack_object` sees it as a key token → `\"Expected format 's', got '%'\"`. Documented in `r282`.\n- Under `JSON_VALIDATE_ONLY` a correct caller must pass **keys only**; interleaving unconsumed value targets shifts the vararg walk (the C then `strlen()`s a target pointer). Tests that need the big multi-key formats pass keys only and assert the value block stays poisoned; the same-arg-list asymmetry is proved with single-key and array formats instead.\n- A negative `s#` length is well defined (not an OOB read): it widens to a huge `size_t` which `strbuffer_append_bytes`'s overflow guard rejects before any `memcpy`, giving `<internal>` / \"Out of memory\". Covered.\n\n## Bugs suspected in files I was told not to edit: none\n\n`value.rs` (`json_vsprintf`, `keylen_foreach`), `load.rs` and `dump.rs` behaved identically to the C on every input these tests reached, including 30-key `JSON_STRICT` unrecognized-key iteration order (which depends on `keylen_foreach` matching `json_object_keylen_foreach`) and >160-byte error-text truncation in `jsonp_error_vset`.\n\n## CONFIGS.md\n\nRows **227–283** (all 57 `pack_unpack.c` rows in section C) flipped from `[ ]` to `[x]`. Verified programmatically that exactly those 57 rows changed and nothing outside the range was touched by me."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":921,"cache_read_input_tokens":321204,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":921,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01VG6vBbkZAs1dk53yKz68VS","session_id":"e1728859-25d0-4463-adf4-96231e8435a5","uuid":"d595818b-6afa-4095-ab1e-4cd69390d0ab","timestamp":"2026-08-31T04:48:19.327Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Phase B tests for pack_unpack.c"}
