ry position (key, value, array element, top level), unterminated `{`/`[`, `\"Expected format 's', got ...\"`, garbage after the format string, tokens after `!`/`*`, and `!`/`*` misplacement.\n- **Type mismatches** for every unpack conversion char against all 8 json types, plus a NULL root and a root with an out-of-range type tag.\n- **Index/key errors**: `json_error_index_out_of_range` for short arrays, `json_error_item_not_found` for missing object keys (and the interaction with `?`).\n\nAlso cover the generic FFI boundaries even where ERRORS.md has no row: NULL format string, empty format string, NULL root, NULL `json_error_t*` (must be tolerated on every entry point), and FLAG WORDS WITH UNDEFINED BITS SET (0x4, 0x8, 0x10, `SIZE_MAX`, and random 64-bit words) — `size_t flags` accepts any value and both implementations must ignore unknown bits identically.\n\nCover the `v*` entry points too — `json_vpack_ex`, `json_vunpack_ex`, `json_vsprintf` — on their ERROR paths specifically, via the `vashim()` trampolines. The C does `va_copy`, so the early-return error path is exactly where vararg handling bugs hide.\n\nIf a row is genuinely unreachable in-process (a live `assert()`/SIGABRT, a segfault, or dead code), add a clearly-commented `#[test]` documenting WHY, quoting the C, and verifying through the FFI the guard that makes it unreachable — then mark that ERRORS.md row `[-] <reason>` instead of `[x]`. Do not fake a passing assertion.\n\nSTEP 3 — run: `cd translation && cargo build --release && timeout 600 cargo test --release --test a14_errors_pack_unpack 2>&1 | tail -40`. Iterate to green.\n\nSTEP 4 — on ANY divergence, fix `translation/src/pack_unpack.rs` (or `varargs.rs`) to match the C exactly, `cargo build --release`, re-run, and ALSO re-run `cargo test --release --test a08_pack_unpack` to confirm no regression.\n\nSTEP 5 — in `translation/ERRORS.md`, change the `verified` cell from `[ ]` to `[x]` for each assigned row that now passes (or `[-] <reason>`). Touch ONLY your assigned row numbers (87, 88, 221-280).\n\nReport: test count, pass/fail, every Rust bug fixed with file and before/after, every row marked `[-]` and why, any bug you suspect lies elsewhere, and how you validated the tests are not vacuous (e.g. by temporarily injecting a bug into pack_unpack.rs, confirming failures, then reverting).","uuid":"8bf7f384-5ed3-48c3-9251-ba0ccd5a952e","session_id":"e1728859-25d0-4463-adf4-96231e8435a5"}
