{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01A9xiSfWvmFdJL2CebCEMLg","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t/*\n2\t * va_list trampoline for the differential tests.\n3\t *\n4\t * Three jansson entry points take a `va_list` rather than `...`:\n5\t *   json_vpack_ex, json_vunpack_ex, json_vsprintf   (plus jsonp_error_vset)\n6\t *\n7\t * Rust on stable cannot *construct* a va_list, but it can call a C variadic\n8\t * function. So each shim below is variadic on the Rust-facing side, turns its\n9\t * arguments into a real va_list, and forwards that to whichever\n10\t * implementation's function pointer it is handed. That lets the tests drive the\n11\t * v* symbols of BOTH libraries with identical arguments.\n12\t *\n13\t * This file lives under translation/tests/ and is compiled into its own\n14\t * separate .so; nothing in c_src/ is touched.\n15\t */\n16\t\n17\t#include <stdarg.h>\n18\t#include <stddef.h>\n19\t\n20\ttypedef struct json_t json_t;\n21\ttypedef struct json_error_t json_error_t;\n22\t\n23\ttypedef json_t *(*vpack_fn)(json_error_t *, size_t, const char *, va_list);\n24\ttypedef int (*vunpack_fn)(json_t *, json_error_t *, size_t, const char *, va_list);\n25\ttypedef json_t *(*vsprintf_fn)(const char *, va_list);\n26\ttypedef void (*verror_fn)(json_error_t *, int, int, size_t, int, const char *, va_list);\n27\t\n28\tjson_t *shim_vpack_ex(void *fn, json_error_t *error, size_t flags, const char *fmt, ...) {\n29\t    va_list ap;\n30\t    json_t *ret;\n31\t    va_start(ap, fmt);\n32\t    ret = ((vpack_fn)fn)(error, flags, fmt, ap);\n33\t    va_end(ap);\n34\t    return ret;\n35\t}\n36\t\n37\tint shim_vunpack_ex(void *fn, json_t *root, json_error_t *error, size_t flags,\n38\t                    const char *fmt, ...) {\n39\t    va_list ap;\n40\t    int ret;\n41\t    va_start(ap, fmt);\n42\t    ret = ((vunpack_fn)fn)(root, error, flags, fmt, ap);\n43\t    va_end(ap);\n44\t    return ret;\n45\t}\n46\t\n47\tjson_t *shim_vsprintf(void *fn, const char *fmt, ...) {\n48\t    va_list ap;\n49\t    json_t *ret;\n50\t    va_start(ap, fmt);\n51\t    ret = ((vsprintf_fn)fn)(fmt, ap);\n52\t    va_end(ap);\n53\t    return ret;\n54\t}\n55\t\n56\tvoid shim_error_vset(void *fn, json_error_t *error, int line, int column, size_t position,\n57\t                     int code, const char *msg, ...) {\n58\t    va_list ap;\n59\t    va_start(ap, msg);\n60\t    ((verror_fn)fn)(error, line, column, position, code, msg, ap);\n61\t    va_end(ap);\n62\t}\n63\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_013ioknR3uh5BBsa6ebVj2DJ","session_id":"e1728859-25d0-4463-adf4-96231e8435a5","uuid":"5b83e9b1-2c83-43c7-a9ab-3a888a99f13c","timestamp":"2026-08-31T04:59:41.768Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Phase C error tests for pack_unpack"}
