{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ovmlfk74bsu6pg2qto64rgqel5ypr4fnotsqu7en3u67ap4hlkwq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All four Phase D gates pass. **398 tests across 16 binaries, 0 failures.**\n\n## Gate results\n\n| Criterion | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` — `nm -D` parity | **130/130**, 0 missing, 0 extra, 0 undefined non-libc |\n| Phase B — every `CONFIGS.md` row | **407/407** (406 verified + 1 documented-unreachable) |\n| Phase C — every `ERRORS.md` row | **356/356** (338 verified + 18 documented-unreachable) |\n| Every feature combination | `Cargo.toml` has no `[features]` — the default build is the only configuration |\n\n## Two real translation bugs found and fixed\n\n1. **`src/dtoa.rs`, `gethex` underflow rounding** — the `Round_up`/`Round_down` sign tests were inverted. C: `case Round_up: if (sign) break; goto ret_tiny;`. So `gethex(\"0x1p-999999999999\", Round_up, sign=0)` gave `0.0` where C gives the smallest denormal.\n\n2. **`src/dump.rs`, `do_dump`** — unwrapped the callback *before* the NULL check, so `json_dump_callback(NULL, NULL, d, JSON_ENCODE_ANY)` panicked instead of returning `-1`; under `panic = \"abort\"` that killed the process.\n\n## Two harness bugs that masqueraded as translation bugs\n\nWorth flagging because both initially looked like real divergences:\n\n- **My `gethex` declaration returned `int`; it returns `void`.** Both sides were reading garbage. Also: `gethex` does `s0 = *sp + 2` with no length check, so a string shorter than `\"0x\"` reads out of bounds — UB in the C, so I removed that input rather than \"fixing\" the Rust to match heap garbage.\n- **dtoa's `Balloc`/`Bfree` freelist is global and non-thread-safe** (`dtoa.c` compiles without `MULTIPLE_THREADS`). Under parallel test threads the **C** side returned plausible-but-wrong digits — e.g. `904692889061487.1882` dumping as `200000000000000.0`. Every test now takes a `global_state_lock()`, so results don't depend on `--test-threads`.\n\nI also added a staleness guard: `cargo test --test <name>` does *not* rebuild the `cdylib` (tests `dlopen` it rather than link it), so the harness now refuses to run against a `.so` older than `src/`. Without that, a fix or regression can silently go untested.\n\n## Confidence in the tests themselves\n\nGreen output alone isn't evidence, so each area was validated by injecting bugs into the Rust and confirming failures, then reverting — 8 mutations in `value.rs` (all caught), the `/` escape in `dump.rs` (10 of 23 failed), a decode flag bit in `load.rs` (7 failed), and two rounds in `pack_unpack.rs` (7, then 27 of 32 failed — confirming the code-byte, line/column/position and `source` comparison channels all bite).\n\nArtifacts: `SYMBOLS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `VERIFICATION.md`, `tests/HARNESS.md`, plus `run_tests.sh` and `status.sh`. Nothing in `c_src/` was modified.\n\nOne caveat on the 19 `[-]` rows: they are *documented-unreachable*, not verified. They're UB in the C, live `assert()` aborts, or dead code — a test could only show both sides crash, which proves nothing about equivalence. For each I verified the *guard* that makes it unreachable instead, with the reason recorded inline."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":668,"cache_read_input_tokens":402548,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":668,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e1728859-25d0-4463-adf4-96231e8435a5","uuid":"a2720610-5221-4f2c-bf43-b8af1b76bf70","timestamp":"2026-08-31T05:40:16.256Z"}
